:: LastChildhoodEvening [childhood]
# One Last Night

You join the other children your age for what feels like a special moment - the last evening you'll all be considered children together. Tomorrow's ceremony will change your status in the tribe, moving you into a different group with different expectations.

Your friends seem to sense this too. The usual games have a bittersweet quality tonight, played with extra enthusiasm but also with an awareness that things are changing.

<<if $relationships.bestFriend > 60>>
Your best friend, <<if $language eq "proto-indo-european">><<if $character.gender eq "female">>Pria<<else>>Agnis<</if>><<elseif $language eq "proto-uralic">><<if $character.gender eq "female">>Aino<<else>>Sampo<</if>><<else>><<if $character.gender eq "female">>Nefert<<else>>Khenti<</if>><</if>>, sits beside you. "We'll still be friends when we're grown, won't we?" <<if $character.gender eq "female">>she<<else>>he<</if>> asks.

"Always," you promise. "Even when we're old like the elders."
<</if>>

<<if $relationships.rival < 50>>
You notice your rival, <<if $language eq "proto-indo-european">><<if $character.gender eq "female">>Mori<<else>>Wlkwos<</if>><<elseif $language eq "proto-uralic">><<if $character.gender eq "female">>Kivi<<else>>Karhu<</if>><<else>><<if $character.gender eq "female">>Bastet<<else>>Sobek<</if>><</if>>, watching from nearby. There's a different look in <<if $character.gender eq "female">>her<<else>>his<</if>> eyes tonight - less hostile, more thoughtful. Perhaps the coming transition has softened the rivalry, or perhaps you're both simply growing up.
<</if>>

As the evening progresses, some of the older children who have already undergone their ceremonies come to share stories about what to expect. Their advice is part serious, part teasing - clearly enjoying their slightly elevated status.

"The ceremony isn't as scary as they make it sound," one whispers. "Just don't forget the words you're supposed to say."

Another adds, "The best part is after - when you're not a child anymore, but not quite grown. It's the perfect time."

<<link "Return to your family's shelter for the night">>
  <<goto "NightBeforeCeremony">>
<</link>>